# Abiotic iron sulfide formation, second order in both reactants:
#
#     Fe(2+) + HS(-)  =  FeS + H(+)
#
# This file is pointed at by <abiotic_file>, NOT <expressions_file>. The difference is which
# sweep runs it: an <expressions_file> law belongs to an organism and only fires in voxels that
# hold that organism's biomass, while this one fires in every fluid voxel. For a reaction that
# happens in open water whether or not anything is alive nearby, this is the one you want.
#
# Two rules follow from having no organism, and both are enforced at load rather than ignored:
#   - every variable must be a substrate; a biomass name here is a stop
#   - there is no "growth" rate; a growth line here is a stop

units  per_second
vars   Fe HS

rate   Fe = -1.6e2 * Fe * HS
rate   HS = -1.6e2 * Fe * HS

range  Fe 1e-9 1e-3
range  HS 1e-9 1e-3
